TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"authorizedComments":[{"author":"uid:1000","body":"PRE-DISPATCH STEER (overseer, arm-time — fold into your first brief). Semantic traps your grep gate cannot catch; all are hard requirements: (1) NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME must be COMPUTED from `ip -br addr` — only rails that actually carry a routable IP. Rail 1 (thunderbolt1) is trained but IP-UNCONFIGURED (169.254.x link-local, no peer): hardcoding both rails passes the grep and hangs RCCL bootstrap. In practice only thunderbolt0 (10.99.0.x /30) qualifies. (2) NCCL_IB_DISABLE=1 UNCONDITIONALLY in host/fn-env.sh — not conditional on device detection. ibverbs devices exist on BOTH nodes by design (usb4_rdma0 + usb4_rdma5); without the pin RCCL autodetects verbs and silently rides the unproven RDMA path. Sockets are the transport of record this run. (3) NEVER export a probe-read engine default: VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM, VLLM_MOE_USE_DEEP_GEMM, VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER* are read via is_set() probes — exporting the default diverts the oracle into a hard raise (spec F.9). (4) Receipts must match scripts/receipts-verify.py EXACTLY — run it against your own output before declaring done. (5) Worker-side actions ride the ethernet wire (10.99.9.2), never a 10.99.0.x Thunderbolt rail — rails carry tensors only. (6) cluster-up is reap-then-gate: reap stale processes first, then gate on health, in that order.","createdAt":"2026-08-29T06:05:30.106Z","id":1,"updatedAt":"2026-08-29T06:05:30.106Z","url":"local://campaign/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering/1"}],"receipt":{"lateRecheckCommentIds":[],"preparedCommentIds":[1],"recheckTruncated":false,"rechecked":true,"source":{"kind":"local-jsonl","path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering-v1.jsonl","preparedCursor":4,"recheckedCursor":4,"registrationId":"01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae"}},"taskId":"host-tooling"}
